---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../data/site';

// TODO(owner): set the real date when the reviewed terms go live, fill the
// governing-law placeholder in section 13 (General), and remove the review banner
// below once an Australian solicitor has signed these off.
const lastUpdated = '26 September 2026';
---
<Layout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern use of the MSRM website and restaurant management platform."
>
  <section class="container-x py-16 max-w-3xl">
    <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="h2 mt-2">Terms of Service</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-mute mt-3 text-sm">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <!-- TEMPLATE BANNER — remove after legal review -->
    <div class="mt-6 rounded-xl border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900">
      <strong>Template — review by an Australian solicitor before launch.</strong>
      These terms are a professionally structured template, not legal advice. Have them
      reviewed and adapted to your circumstances before relying on them.
    </div>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-ink-soft leading-relaxed">
      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">1. Agreement to these terms</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the {SITE.name} website and
          the {SITE.name} restaurant management platform, apps and related services
          (together, the "Service"), provided by {SITE.name} ("we", "us", "our"). By
          accessing the website or creating an account, you agree to these Terms. If you
          use the Service on behalf of a business, you represent that you are authorised
          to bind that business, and "you" refers to it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">2. The Service</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Service is a subscription software platform for hospitality businesses —
          including point of sale, kitchen display, inventory, online ordering,
          integrations and reporting. We may improve, add or change features over time;
          we will not materially reduce the core functionality of your paid plan during a
          paid period without notice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">3. Accounts</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>You must provide accurate account and business information and keep it current;</li>
          <li>You are responsible for safeguarding login credentials and for all activity under your account, including staff users you create;</li>
          <li>You must notify us promptly of any unauthorised use of your account.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">4. Licence and intellectual property</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We grant you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable licence to use the
          Service for your internal business purposes during your subscription. We (and
          our licensors) retain all intellectual property rights in the Service, its
          software, design and content. You retain all rights in the data you and your
          staff enter into the Service ("Your Data"); you grant us a licence to host and
          process Your Data solely to provide and improve the Service.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">5. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">You must not, and must not permit anyone to:</p>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Use the Service in breach of any law, or to store or transmit unlawful, infringing or harmful material;</li>
          <li>Interfere with or disrupt the Service, probe or test its security, or attempt to gain unauthorised access to it or its data;</li>
          <li>Reverse engineer, copy, resell, sublicense or make the Service available to third parties except as we expressly permit;</li>
          <li>Use the Service to send spam or misleading communications;</li>
          <li>Exceed reasonable usage or circumvent plan limits.</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-2">We may suspend access where we reasonably believe this section has been breached, giving notice where practicable.</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">6. Fees and billing</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>Subscription fees are charged per outlet, in Australian dollars, at the rates published on our <a href="/pricing" class="text-brand-700 underline">pricing page</a> or agreed in writing. Prices are inclusive or exclusive of GST as stated at checkout;</li>
          <li>Fees are billed in advance for each billing period and, except as required by law (including the Australian Consumer Law) or expressly stated, are non-refundable;</li>
          <li>We may change fees with at least 30 days' notice; changes apply from your next billing period;</li>
          <li>If payment fails, we may retry, and may suspend the Service after reasonable notice until payment is made;</li>
          <li>Any free trial converts to a paid subscription only if you choose a plan; we will not silently start charging you.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">7. Your Data and privacy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Our collection and handling of personal information is described in our
          <a href="/privacy" class="text-brand-700 underline">Privacy Policy</a>. You are
          responsible for having a lawful basis (and any required notices or consents) for
          the customer and staff data you enter into the Service. You can export Your Data
          during your subscription and for 30 days after termination, after which we may
          delete it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">8. Third-party services</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The Service integrates with third-party products — such as delivery
          marketplaces, payment terminals and processors, and accounting software. Those
          services are governed by their own terms, and we are not responsible for their
          acts, omissions, fees or availability. An integration failing because of a
          third-party change is not a breach of these Terms, though we will use reasonable
          efforts to restore it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">9. Availability and support</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          We aim for high availability but do not guarantee the Service will be
          uninterrupted or error-free. Planned maintenance will be scheduled outside peak
          trading hours where practicable. Offline features are designed to keep core POS
          functions running during connectivity loss, but depend on your local hardware
          and configuration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">10. Consumer guarantees and disclaimers</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Nothing in these Terms excludes, restricts or modifies any consumer guarantee,
          right or remedy under the Australian Consumer Law or other law that cannot
          lawfully be excluded. Subject to that, the Service is provided "as is" and we
          exclude all other conditions, warranties and guarantees, whether express or
          implied. Where our liability for breach of a non-excludable guarantee can be
          limited, it is limited (at our option) to resupplying the Service or paying the
          cost of resupply.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">11. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          To the maximum extent permitted by law: (a) neither party is liable for
          indirect or consequential loss, loss of profits, revenue, goodwill or data; and
          (b) our total aggregate liability arising out of or in connection with the
          Service is limited to the fees you paid us in the 12 months before the event
          giving rise to the claim. These limits do not apply to liability that cannot be
          limited by law, or to your obligation to pay fees.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">12. Termination</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5">
          <li>You may cancel at any time from your account or by written notice; cancellation takes effect at the end of the current billing period. There is no lock-in contract;</li>
          <li>Either party may terminate immediately for a material breach that is not remedied within 14 days of written notice, or if the other party becomes insolvent;</li>
          <li>On termination, your right to use the Service ends; sections that by their nature should survive (including fees owed, IP, liability limits and governing law) survive.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">13. General</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These Terms are governed by the laws of
          <strong>[State/Territory — e.g. Victoria], Australia</strong>, and the parties
          submit to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of its courts.
          <!-- TODO(owner): set the governing state/territory before launch. -->
          We may update these Terms from time to time; material changes will be notified
          to account holders by email at least 30 days before taking effect, and continued
          use after that date constitutes acceptance. If any provision is unenforceable,
          the rest remain in force. You may not assign these Terms without our consent; we
          may assign them as part of a corporate restructure or sale of the business.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink">14. Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          Questions about these Terms:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-brand-700 underline">{SITE.email}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm"><a href="/" class="text-brand-700 underline">← Back home</a></p>
  </section>
</Layout>
